      "body": "- [x] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do?\n\nModelOpt pruning needs a hybrid model whose MoE experts use separate linear layers instead of grouped GEMM. This change adds a statically composed `hybrid_stack_spec_no_moe_grouped_gemm` next to the existing grouped-GEMM spec.\n\nCallers choose the named spec at model construction time, so the exact implementation remains visible from the module spec and does not switch from a runtime boolean. The existing `hybrid_stack_spec` behavior is unchanged. ModelOpt now reuses the shared static spec instead of maintaining a partial duplicate, and the Mamba compatibility name is retained.\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nFixes #4106\n\n## Contribution process\n\n### Pre-checks\n\n- [x] I have added relevant unit tests\n- [ ] I have added relevant functional tests\n- [x] I have added proper typing to my code [Typing guidelines](https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html)\n- [ ] I have added relevant documentation\n- [ ] I have run the [autoformatter.sh](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/blob/main/tools/autoformat.sh) on my PR\n\n### Validation\n\n- Unit coverage verifies the fixed non-grouped MoE composition, preserved neighboring hybrid layers, and Mamba compatibility alias.\n- `python3 -m py_compile`, Black 26.3.0, isort 5.13.2, `git diff --check`, and a static-spec contract check passed.\n- The repaired design follows `megatron/core/models/hybrid/AGENTS.md`: no CLI, configuration, or runtime boolean selects behavior inside `hybrid_layer_specs.py`.\n\nThe repaired commit is rebased on current `main` and signed. Runtime GPU-dependent model tests remain a hosted CI gate.\n",
